        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Stomacher of embroidered linen in silks, bound with silk tape, made in England, 1700-1729"@en , "Linen stomacher bound with silk tape. With a floral design embroidered with coloured silks in long and short, satin, stem, chain and back stitches. Background pattern of scrolls worked in silk in back stitch. Presumably for a child. Backed with cotton. Three silk tapes on either side and five radiating tabs at the bottom."@en ;
